# CineLog has NO server-side environment variables and no build step.
#
# How the TMDB token works in this project:
#   - CineLog needs a TMDB API Read Access Token. It belongs to the VISITOR:
#     anyone can get one free at themoviedb.org -> Settings -> API.
#   - The visitor pastes it into the app's setup panel. It is stored ONLY in
#     that visitor's browser localStorage and is sent ONLY to
#     api.themoviedb.org as an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header.
#   - There is deliberately NO token in this repository. Never commit one.
#
# Production alternative (see README): a tiny serverless proxy (Vercel /
# Netlify function) that holds the token server-side and forwards an
# allowlist of TMDB paths, so visitors need no token of their own.
